Ladybird opens at most six connections to a host at once for fetches,
and doesn’t count WebSockets toward that limit. The other engines all
limit a host to six connections the same way. Chromium does it with its
g_max_sockets_per_group for the normal socket pool, and gives WebSockets
a separate pool limited to 255. Gecko does it with the pref named
network.http.max-persistent-connections-per-server. And WebKit sets its
kHTTPLoadWidth limit to 6 in initializeNetworkSettings(), in the file
NetworkProcessCocoa.mm, and its curl port uses the same value through
CurlDefaultMaxHostConnections.
